# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is required: an empty or
# missing value means this build cannot do that one thing, and the app says so in
# plain language rather than half-working.
#
# `apps/desktop/electron.vite.config.ts` loads this file and substitutes the
# values into the main-process bundle at BUILD time. It has to be build time: an
# app launched from Finder inherits launchd's minimal environment, so anything
# read from `process.env` at runtime is empty in a packaged build.
#
# That means the dmg carries whatever was in this file when it was built. Rebuild
# after changing anything here. Real environment variables beat this file, so a
# one-off `QALE_POSTHOG_DEV=1 pnpm dev` still overrides.

# PostHog Cloud EU (docs/telemetry-posthog.md). The project key is write-only and
# meant to ship in clients. Empty = this build has no sender at all, which is the
# right default for a dev machine.
QALE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Only set this to point somewhere other than https://eu.i.posthog.com. The EU
# host is the hardcoded default so a missing value can never fall back to US.
QALE_POSTHOG_HOST=
# `1` stamps every event and person as dev, so our own runs are obvious in a
# project shared with the beta. Never set this in a build you hand to someone.
QALE_POSTHOG_DEV=

# Google Cloud OAuth client for Calendar (docs/google-cloud-setup.md). The
# "secret" for an installed app is officially non-confidential — the loopback +
# PKCE flow is what actually protects the grant. Empty = the Connections screen
# says this build has no Google client configured, and offers nothing to click.
QALE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
QALE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Used by dev tooling and the agent in development, not baked into the binary:
# the app itself is bring-your-own-key, entered in Settings.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
